A||N||8||WhiteFieroBlur||Oil and Gas treatments||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||10-25-2001||11:16 AM||||I was wondering, what kind of treatments does everyone use on thier fiero. Wheather it be in the engine or gas. Which stuff is the good stuff and which stuff have you found out is not so good. I am about to change my oil and want to put some kind of engine treatment in so what should I use that you have found out to be the best. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-25-2001||11:18 AM||||My Dad has ocassionally used Slick50 in his 88GT, I just run synthetic oil (AmsOil if available).  I also just used a bottle of injector cleaner (castrol brand?) and it worked wonders!||||reg||1
Z||000002||WhiteFieroBlur||10-25-2001||12:13 PM||||How is the synthetic oil? If I never used this oil can I go ahead and change over to it? I have been wanting to use this oil but heard its good for certain types of cars and wondered if it works great in our car than the other oils.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||10-25-2001||12:36 PM||||As long as you're not breaking in a new motor, go ahead and switch to synthetic.  Just like changing normal oil- drain the old, change the filter, replace with new (synthetic) oil.  Amsoil has a program where you change the filter more often than the oil  itself... I don't know the details, but you can check with a local Amsoil rep.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BlackStang95||10-25-2001||12:37 PM||||Synthetic protects much better during cold starts and a little better all the time, don't expect a performance increase though, and still change it on time.  I've heard that once you start using synthetic if you then switch back your car will have lots of problems.  So, make sure you can afford the extra expense ($5 a quart instead of $1.10 in my area). <P>As for treatments STP is my brand of choice, every couple thousands miles I use fuel injector cleaner.  Again don't expect performance, it's just a preventative maitnance thing really.||||reg||1
Z||000005||SLYGUY||10-25-2001||03:28 PM||||I used a bottle of STP fuel system cleaner and noticed the difference immediately. Right away the car started better, ran smoother and the 103K mile old engine feels great. The power is much stronger, response is immediate, and has a nice smooth idle.<BR>I thought it was gonna be $7 thrown away but I was very surprised.<P>Since I bought the car a month ago I changed:<BR>Oil and filters<BR>Tranny fluid<BR>EGR sensor<BR>O2 sensor<BR>spark plugs <BR>cap and rotor<BR>Clutch master cylinder<P>Car ran better with each item and runs like new now.<BR>Heck, it was even fun.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000006||88CoupeV6||10-25-2001||06:50 PM||||Crankcase:<BR>I use moble one oil, I also add about a cup of <B>marvel mystery oil</B>.<P>Gas:<BR>STP fuel injecter cleaner at every oil change. and 4 Oz. of <B>marvel mystery oil</B> every other fillup. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">     <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A><p>[This message has been edited by 88CoupeV6 (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000007||rogergarrison||10-25-2001||07:18 PM||||I use castrol synthetic in mine mostly because of the added heat from turbo. It also eliminated any oil burning, I havent had to add between 5K-10K changes for 90,000 miles. only additive i recommend and use is a quality fuel system cleaner in gas tank every month or 2. There all the same stuff, so brand names your choice.<P>I tried Slick 50 in one of my Lincolns when I had a limo service. It immediatly started burning lots of oil, changed back a week later and went back to normal. A friend that works for an oil company said that the problem with some of those type additives is that it makes the rings and cylinder walls so slick, that there is not enough friction between the rings and cylinder to properly seal them, so oil gets into the combustion chamber. If I remember rite, Slick 50 was ordered to stop advertising its supposed advantages by the feds.<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||GTFiero1||10-26-2001||05:00 PM||||got the new GM High-Tech Performance magazine. they tested synthetic oil verses mineral oil. there got a ther got a 2001 Camaro SS with a bone stock engien, they dynoed it with regular mineral oil and got 320.8 rwhp the they put Royal Purple synthetic oil in and dynoed it again, and this time they got 325.4 rwhp. they also tested there highly modded LT1 firebird with similar results. this is the jan 2002 issue<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
